From 5ae90c127a53ff3ff0867e6f0b9ae934b09bd148 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:04:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi3: iOS 10 logd/libdispatch: boot session UUID, activity
 IDs, kevent fixes

- kern.bootsessionuuid sysctl: libsystem_trace aborts without it (logd
  could never start serving).
- Mach trap 43 is mach_generate_activity_id on iOS 10 (map_fd here);
  libdispatch aborts when it fails.
- Undefined instructions: permanently-undefined encodings (Thumb trap,
  ARM UDF) or a fault with VFP already on now raise EXC_BAD_INSTRUCTION
  instead of re-enabling VFP and re-running the instruction forever;
  logged on serial.
- kevent: EV_VANISHED is not echoed back; EVFILT_MACHPORT knotes with no
  message space left wait for the next scan, and too-large messages
  report the buffer and the port name.
- Watchdog prints user backtraces of backboardd/SpringBoard/logd;
  rpi3_dtlog logs every send by the traced program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0123xbco8JF8tibbBMLmXceV
